      "question": "The ratio of three angles of a triangle is 1 : 3 : 5. Which is the measure of the greatest angle?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "80°"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "100​°"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "60​°"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "120​°"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "**Given:**\n\nThe ratio of three angles of a triangle is 1 : 3 : 5.\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nIn triangle,\n\nSum of all angles = 180° \n\n**Explanation:**\n\nLet be the proportional value = x\n\nx + 3x + 5x = 180° \n\n⇒ 9x = 180° \n\n⇒ x = 20° \n\nThe greatest angle = 5x \n\n⇒ 5 × 20° = 100° \n\n**∴ The measure of the greatest angle is 100° .**",
      "tags": [
        "Lines and Angles"
      ]
    },
