      "question": "In ∆ABC, ∠B = 72° and ∠C = 44°, Side BC is produced to D. The bisectors of ∠B and ∠ACD meet at E. what is the measure of ∠BEC?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "36°"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "32°"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "46°"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "58°"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/50d418a7a6e3a7617fe8264eae844efae1b2927e865cb324586de4426f8ffefc.png] \n\n**Short trick:**\n\n∠B = 72° and ∠C = 44°\n\n∠A = 180° – 72° – 44° = 64°\n\n∠BEC = ∠A/2 = 64°/2 = 32°\n\n**Detailed Method:**\n\n⇒ ∠ACD = 180° – ∠C = 180° – 44° = 136°\n\n⇒ ∠ACE = ∠ACD/2 = 136°/2 = 68°\n\n⇒ ∠BCE = ∠BCA + ∠ACE = 44° + 68° = 112°\n\n⇒ ∠EBC = ∠B/2 = 72°/2 = 36°\n\nIn ΔBCE,\n\n∠EBC + ∠BCE + ∠BEC = 180°\n\n⇒ ∠BEC = 180° – 36° – 112° = 32°",
      "solution_images": [
